Return on the go strategies enable convenient product returns integrated into user routines and existing infrastructure rather than requiring dedicated trips to collection centers. By placing return options at convenient locations—retail storefronts, transit hubs, delivery points—companies significantly increase participation rates in take-back programs. Products designed for on-the-go returns must accommodate compact packaging, standardized containers, and rapid handling by non-specialized staff. This approach dramatically improves the feasibility of reuse and refurbishment systems.